# Agent memory resolves relative to cwd. A subagent launched with cwd=apps/web writes a
# from-scratch .claude/agent-memory/ tree there instead of a delta of the real one at the
# repo root — truncated, count-less, and easy to commit by accident next to the stray
# apps/web/.git.disabled-by-claude-* dir. Merge anything useful into the root tree, then
# let this keep FUTURE duplicates out of the index.
#
# Caveat: gitignore does not untrack what is already tracked.
# apps/web/.claude/agent-memory/test-writer/MEMORY.md has been committed since f972b77c
# (Study Mode, #1006) and is unaffected by this rule — removing it is a separate cleanup,
# deliberately not done in a content PR.
apps/web/.claude/

# The stray apps/web/.git.disabled-by-claude-<date>/ dir the comment above refers to. A prior
# session neutralised a nested repo by renaming its .git rather than removing it, leaving ~549
# untracked files under apps/web/. Two costs, and the second is the dangerous one:
#   1. `git add -A apps/web` stages all of them.
#   2. `/fullpush` step 5b aborts the push on ANY untracked path (`git status --porcelain
#      --untracked-files=all`). That gate exists to catch an untracked MIRROR edit — a rule or
#      doc file written but never `git add`ed. Permanent debris makes it fire every time, so the
#      only way to push is to look past it, which is exactly how a real untracked mirror edit
#      gets waved through. A gate that always fails protects nothing.
# Ignoring it, not deleting it: removal of someone else's disabled repo is a separate, explicit
# cleanup. Glob the date suffix — the name carries whenever it was disabled.
# Trailing `/` = directory-only. If a future session ever leaves the artifact as a POINTER FILE
# (as `.git` is under worktrees and submodules) rather than a renamed directory, this will not
# match — which fails SAFE: the file surfaces as untracked rather than being silently swallowed.
apps/web/.git.disabled-by-claude-*/

# Branch-deletion logs written by session cleanup. Local bookkeeping, dated, never repo artifacts.
.claude/deleted-branches-????-??-??.txt

# Two per-issue manual-eval seed scripts, ignored BY NAME. Local scratch for #1011 and #907 —
# never shipped, and they carry hardcoded local credentials. Listed individually rather than as
# `seed-*-eval.ts` on purpose: six eval seeds ARE tracked (seed-quiz-setup-eval.ts,
# seed-vfr-rt-training-eval.ts, seed-dashboard-eval.ts, seed-admin-eval.ts,
# seed-internal-exam-eval.ts, seed-eval.ts) and a glob would silently swallow the next legitimate
# one — gitignore spares them today only because it cannot untrack, which is not a guarantee.
# Why mechanical: a directory-wide `git add apps/web/scripts/` swept these two into a commit FOUR
# times across the VFR RT branches. Each time the fix was "use explicit paths", and it did not
# hold. Use `git add -f` if one ever genuinely needs to ship.
apps/web/scripts/seed-1011-eval.ts
apps/web/scripts/seed-907-pagination-eval.ts

# Local working-document folders — third-party reference material (ISO standards, operator
# manuals), ~15MB of PDFs. Not repo artifacts, and not ours to redistribute. Listed by exact
# name rather than a `/[0-9][0-9]. */` glob on purpose: a glob would silently swallow a future
# numbered directory that IS repo content.
/01. Product Maturity/
/02. AI ELP/
